cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or the derived tables, please cite it, and cite UCDP as described in DATA-RIGHTS.md.
title: "TOCSIN: a conflict-forecasting system with reference-class base rates and calibration scoring"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zajac
    given-names: Kara
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7400-1394"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KaraZajac/TOCSIN"
url: "https://tocsin.karazajac.io"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - conflict forecasting
  - armed conflict
  - base rates
  - reference-class forecasting
  - calibration
  - Brier score
  - forecast combination
  - UCDP
  - VIEWS
abstract: >-
  A conflict-forecasting system whose every probability is a transparent
  reference-class base rate: an explicit ladder (the unit's own history, its
  region, the world) over the UCDP record, conditioned on recency structure,
  with empirical-Bayes shrinkage and the class counts in view; walk-forward
  calibration scoring on ~280k historical unit-years; a journal of
  operational questions with UCDP-pinned criteria that resolve mechanically
  from each data refresh; and a challenger arena scoring other forecasts
  (VIEWS, naive baselines, analyst overrides) against the engine on
  identical resolved outcomes. Evaluated walk-forward on the VIEWS target
  (7,680 country-months, five historical vantages), the system attains
  Brier 0.0461 against VIEWS's 0.0412 — within 12% of the state of the art
  — while five preregistered covariate families (regime type, horizon
  decay, youth bulges, militarized-dispute and alliance history, ethnic
  exclusion) all fail out-of-sample against the recency-conditioned base
  rates. The preprint in paper/ documents the transparency tax, an exact
  metric-blindness decomposition of the Brier score at rare-event base
  rates, and the equal-weight pool that beats every individual model.
  Derived tables and registries are CC BY 4.0, built from UCDP/PRIO and
  other public sources; see DATA-RIGHTS.md for the layered rights and
  required citations.
